.TH KLS 1 "May 2026" "kls 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kls \- a read-only Linux filesystem security auditor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kls
[\fBOPTIONS\fR]... [\fBDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kls
is a read-only Linux filesystem security auditor. It inspects a directory tree, identifies security-relevant conditions, and reports both its findings and the coverage limitations of the audit. It adds rich metadata and alerts regarding potential security risks.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global Options
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color output (useful for logs/pipes).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all non-essential output. Conflicts with \fB\-\-verbose\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable detailed diagnostic logging. Conflicts with \fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR.

.SS Collection & Filtering Options
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Include hidden files and directories (dotfiles).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recursively traverse subdirectories.
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-depth " DEPTH"
Limit recursion depth (requires \fB\-\-recursive\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " PATTERN"
Filter entries by glob pattern (e.g., *.conf).
.TP
.BI \-\-modified\-before " DATE"
Show only files modified before given date (YYYY-MM-DD).
.TP
.BI \-\-modified\-after " DATE"
Show only files modified after given date (YYYY-MM-DD).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-findings
Display only entries with detected security findings.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-severity " SEVERITY"
Filter findings by minimum severity (low|medlow|med|high|crit).
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " SEVERITY"
Exit with code 5 if findings at or above severity exist (low|medlow|med|high|crit).

.SS Sorting Options
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " CRITERIA"
Sort by: name, size, type, modified, ext, findings.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Invert the sorting order.
.TP
.B \-\-dirs\-first
Group directories before files.
.TP
.B \-\-findings\-first
Prioritize entries with findings at the top.

.SS Presentation Options
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long
Detailed list format (permissions, owner, size, mtime).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-header
Omit table headers from the output.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Audit completed successfully (or \fB\-\-help\fR/\fB\-\-version\fR).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Incomplete audit (e.g., permission denied, vanished entries).
.TP
.B 4
Internal failure.
.TP
.B 5
Configured threshold exceeded.

.SH EXAMPLES
Audit the current directory:
.IP
.B kls
.PP
Recursively audit a directory, showing only entries with findings:
.IP
.B kls --recursive --only-findings /var/log
.PP
Audit a directory and fail if any high or critical severity findings exist:
.IP
.B kls --fail-on=high /etc

